    {"symbol": "⚓", "tooltip": "Strict liability is like an anchor; it holds safety commitments in place when competitive currents pull developers toward faster release. But if the anchor is too heavy for small boats, does it sink the fleet or just steady the tankers?"},
    {"symbol": "🧱", "tooltip": "Layered AI governance is like a load-bearing wall; pre-deployment gates and strict liability each carry weight the other cannot. But which brick fails first when a frontier model causes irreversible harm — the gate that didn't catch it, or the liability that can't undo it?"}
  ],
